{
  "name": "Why the decision matrix",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Run this\n\nClick **Execute workflow**.\n\nFive requests go through **Intake policy**. Open that node and read the output table: one ruleset, five different actions. The Switch only fans out the action the matrix already chose.\n\nThen open **Raised bar**. It is the same five requests and the same rules. The only change is a Thresholds row: `medium_confidence` moves from 0.7 to 0.99. The README typo stops being automatic. The outage still pages, because that rule uses `high_confidence` and blast radius, which this knob does not touch.",
        "height": 280,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "b1d0e6a0-0001-4000-8000-000000000001",
      "name": "How to read this",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [-40, -40]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## One ruleset, first match\n\nThe node asks four questions: work type, blast radius, needs design, needs a human. It walks the rules in order and stops at the first hit.\n\n1. Confident incident and blast radius ≥ `wide_blast` (2) → page on-call. `gate` is true.\n2. Needs design ≥ `medium_confidence` (0.7), or blast radius ≥ 2 → hold for design. `gate` is true.\n3. Bugfix or feature, confidence ≥ `medium_confidence`, blast radius < 2, no design signal, no human signal → implementer.\n4. Anything else → a person. That includes a low-confidence guess at \"bugfix\".\n\nThe comparisons name the thresholds. A later item can override one number without editing the policy.",
        "height": 340,
        "width": 500,
        "color": 5
      },
      "id": "b1d0e6a0-0001-4000-8000-000000000002",
      "name": "The policy",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [460, -40]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## The same policy as nested IFs\n\nIncident AND confidence ≥ 0.85 AND blast radius ≥ 2 → page.\nElse needs design ≥ 0.7 OR blast radius ≥ 2 → design review.\nElse type is bugfix or feature AND confidence ≥ 0.7 AND blast radius < 2 AND needs design < 0.4 AND needs a human < 0.5 → implementer.\nElse → a person.\n\nEach new question adds another branch. Changing 0.7 means finding every comparison that used it. Here that number is the name `medium_confidence`, and the rule order is the priority.",
        "height": 300,
        "width": 460,
        "color": 6
      },
      "id": "b1d0e6a0-0001-4000-8000-000000000003",
      "name": "What this replaces",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1000, -40]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Where the answers come from\n\nThe compose stand-in maps phrases in the state to fixed answers: checkout is down, migrate, not sure / maybe, typo / README, make it better. A real System One server would score these same four questions. The rules do not change between those two.\n\nPinned on **Requests**, in order:\n1. Checkout is down → page on-call\n2. Migrate the payments schema → hold for design\n3. Maybe a bug, not sure → a person (the type is bugfix, the confidence is 0.48)\n4. Typo in the README → implementer\n5. Make the app better → a person",
        "height": 320,
        "width": 460
      },
      "id": "b1d0e6a0-0001-4000-8000-000000000004",
      "name": "The five requests",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [1500, -40]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {},
      "id": "b1d0e6a0-0001-4000-8000-000000000010",
      "name": "Requests",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.manualTrigger",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [200, 460]
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "state": "={{ $json.state }}",
        "questionSet": "custom",
        "questions": {
          "work_type": {
            "type": "choice",
            "instructions": "What kind of work is this",
            "criteria": {
              "incident": "Customers are blocked or a service is down",
              "bugfix": "Correct broken behavior, small and specific",
              "feature": "New behavior or a structural change",
              "unclear": "The request does not say what to do"
            }
          },
          "blast_radius": {
            "type": "score",
            "instructions": "How wide is the blast radius if we act on this",
            "criteria": [
              "One file or a copy change",
              "One feature, easy to reverse",
              "Shared data or several services",
              "Payments, security, or hard to reverse"
            ]
          },
          "needs_design": {
            "type": "noul",
            "instructions": "A design review should happen before anyone implements this"
          },
          "needs_human": {
            "type": "noul",
            "instructions": "A person should look at this before any automated action"
          }
        },
        "rules": {
          "version": 1,
          "default_action": {
            "type": "escalate",
            "target": "human",
            "reason": "Not confident enough to act on {{answers.work_type.choice}} ({{answers.work_type.confidence}})"
          },
          "thresholds": {
            "high_confidence": 0.85,
            "medium_confidence": 0.7,
            "wide_blast": 2
          },
          "rules": [
            {
              "id": "page-incident",
              "description": "A confident incident with a wide blast radius pages on-call",
              "when": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "question": "work_type",
                    "eq": "incident",
                    "confidence_gte": "high_confidence"
                  },
                  { "question": "blast_radius", "gte": "wide_blast" }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "page",
                "target": "oncall",
                "reason": "Incident, blast radius {{answers.blast_radius.score}}",
                "gate": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "hold-for-design",
              "description": "A wide blast radius or a design signal is held before implementation",
              "when": {
                "any": [
                  { "question": "needs_design", "gte": "medium_confidence" },
                  { "question": "blast_radius", "gte": "wide_blast" }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "review",
                "target": "design",
                "reason": "Hold for design. Blast radius {{answers.blast_radius.score}}, needs_design {{answers.needs_design.noul}}",
                "gate": true
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "ship-it",
              "description": "A confident, narrow bugfix or feature can go to an implementer",
              "when": {
                "all": [
                  {
                    "question": "work_type",
                    "in": ["bugfix", "feature"],
                    "confidence_gte": "medium_confidence"
                  },
                  { "question": "blast_radius", "lt": "wide_blast" },
                  { "question": "needs_design", "lt": 0.4 },
                  { "question": "needs_human", "lt": 0.5 }
                ]
              },
              "action": {
                "type": "route",
                "target": "implementer",
                "reason": "Ship as {{answers.work_type.choice}}. Blast radius {{answers.blast_radius.score}}",
                "gate": false
              }
            }
          ]
        },
        "options": {
          "timeout": 60000,
          "includeFullAnswers": true,
          "failOnNoMatch": false
        }
      },
